<item><title>Congo seeks Francophonie backing for forest decade and UN Security Council seat</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-seeks-francophonie-backing-for-forest-decade-and-un-626fa5/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-seeks-francophonie-backing-for-forest-decade-and-un-626fa5/</guid><category>Republic of Congo</category><description>Brazzaville asked member states at a ministerial meeting in Cambodia to support a UN forestry decade, a cultural heritage bid and a 2030-2031 Security Council place.</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:52:24 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cg.jpg" length="37606" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Congo resumes government evaluation seminars after two-year pause</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-resumes-government-evaluation-seminars-after-two-year-68f3c0/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-resumes-government-evaluation-seminars-after-two-year-68f3c0/</guid><category>Republic of Congo</category><description>The eighth seminar, opened in Brazzaville on 13 November by Prime Minister Anatole Collinet Makosso, reviews three planning documents that set priorities to 2031 and beyond.</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:53:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-resumes-government-evaluation-seminars-after-two-year-68f3c0/share.jpg" length="44642" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-resumes-government-evaluation-seminars-after-two-year-68f3c0/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Congo must beat Comoros at home to keep CAN 2027 hopes alive</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-must-beat-comoros-at-home-to-keep-can-2027-hopes-alive-2ac76b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-must-beat-comoros-at-home-to-keep-can-2027-hopes-alive-2ac76b/</guid><category>Republic of Congo</category><description>The Red Devils drew 0-0 in Moroni and now host the Comoros in Brazzaville on Tuesday, needing a win to lift their total to five points.</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:31:32 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cg.jpg" length="37606" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
